      "notes": "Students may use twelve units of CSE 190 toward CSE elective credit (CSE 291 counts toward this maximum). Up to eight units of ENG 100D/L toward upper-division CSE elective/technical elective credits; ENG 100D only once. A maximum of twelve units of P/NP courses may count, chosen from: a maximum of eight units of CSE 198 or 199 or 199H; a maximum of four units of CSE 197; a maximum of two units of CSE 109. A maximum of four units of special studies course work may count from the following: CSE 197, CSE 198, CSE 199, CSE 199H, ENG 100D, or ENG 100L. Undergraduate students may petition to use graduate-level course work toward their elective requirements. The catalog says \"Five upper-division electives\" but also refers to a \"twenty-four-unit minimum\"; five four-unit courses fit its sixty-four upper-division units."
